  "title": "Provider-neutral tracker seam and the first GitHub adapter",
  "summary": "Adds a new `tracker` module that defines a provider-neutral `Tracker` trait (read ready items, write state, write a recap, report capabilities) plus the ready rule, the run-finishing writes, and an in-memory test double. On top of that seam it lands the first adapter, `github_tracker`, which drives GitHub Issues and Projects v2 through the installed `gh` CLI: every request is one `gh` invocation whose argv and JSON payload are built by pure functions and whose response is read by a pure parser. The adapter verifies the project's status field before reading, pages ready items with a cursor, keeps malformed non-ready items as skipped placeholders, and for a blocked state posts a cause comment before moving the status.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
